  "doctrine": [],
  "note": "The doubled forms describe inward churning in Lamentations 1:20 and 2:11 and a face reddened with weeping in Job 16:16. The source calls their stem pealal. The spelling of the donkey is also Hamor’s name. Hamran (1Ch 1:41) corresponds to Hemdan (Gen 36:26), so its derivation is uncertain. SEDRA 1073 and 1075 distinguish the donkey and wine. An historical connection between the measure, heaping, clay and fermentation is uncertain."
